<h2>The back office</h2>
<p>The toolkit includes the boring systems nobody brags about and every shop needs: inventory tracking for ink, needles, and supplies; expense records alongside your income, so tax season is a report instead of a shoebox; and dashboards that show designers and shop staff exactly what they have earned and what is pending. Payouts require a registered account, an active paid subscription, and a configured payout method — set it up once, at signup, and proceeds flow instead of piling up.</p>

<h2>What it costs, and how to join</h2>
<p>A tattoo shop membership is a single annual subscription — the current price is shown on the <a href="/membership">membership page</a> and in our <a href="/terms">terms</a> — plus the 1% tap-to-pay split described above. There is no separate per-seat pricing in the plan: it is built for working shops, not enterprise software. To join, create an account, choose the shop plan, and set up your storefront; if you want advertising placement beyond the storefront — featured spots and promotions reaching the marketplace audience — see the <a href="/advertise">advertising page</a> as well. Questions before you commit are welcome on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>: pick the shop topic and a human reads it.</p>

<p>And if you are an artist rather than a shop — drawing designs, taking custom commissions, or both — the <a href="/designers/guide">designer guide</a> covers upload specs, style rules, and how the 60% commission works, and the <a href="/guides/custom-design-process">custom design guide</a> shows the client side of the process you would be fulfilling.</p>
